stion and I think  based on your experience and I think I  haven't seen any data that says that  since the inception of X campaign we see  X reduction in texting I don't know what  it's gonna take I really don't you know  I've watched a very very moving short  film about the the carnage literally the  carnage in the wake of people texting  while driving and maybe it should be  mandatory viewing every time we get in  the car I don't know it's just so easy  and so tempting to text as you as you  know the the one of the the National  Safety Board's not nitsa but that the  Accident Investigation Agency the  federal one has called for a complete  and total ban on cellphones in cars  period and I think that that's sort of  extreme but that may be the only  solution to the problem of someone who's  who may literally be addicted to their  smartphone and unable to stop themselves  from texting it is incredible and it'll  be interesting to see as vehicle  technology continues to develop whether  there might be a technology solution to  the issue of texting while driving but  will continue obviously to follow it  we've been speaking with Carol Lok net  features editor for edmunds.com thanks  so much for being on with us today  thanks for having me David

